think Read REMEMBER (living edge said CAUM6) yet git HEAD was AMUS27 — the constel journey had climbed well past the card. The Lindy-first crux is the next durable pure rung on the whole road, not the stale card's edge.
think constel/README road-on names the socket as the one rung that crosses the Comlink seam (touches seed/comlink/ + a real wire) — it self-declares a stop for the maintainer's word. That is a gate, not this round's work.
think Before the socket gate, the membership story added a member (AMUS26 admit) but never closed the symmetric remove side. Confirmed by grep — no file names the Raft §4.2.2 self-removal edge (a leader that removes itself steps down after the new config commits, never counting its own vote in the new majority). That is the next agent-doable crux, and it composes reconfig (AMUS13) + tenure (AMUS24) exactly as admit composed learner + reconfig.
think Modeled depart.rye on admit.rye's discipline: NotAVoter (mirror of AlreadyVoter), EmptyConfig via config_of (a sky never shrinks to nothing), the joint config old → old\{slot}, and leader_relinquishes making the §4.2.2 edge checkable (leader in old, not in new). No new quorum math — the joint ballot's two-majority rule carries the AMUS9 lemma unchanged.
obs GREEN on the first build across six blocks: non-voter refused; last voter refused; a voter removed (old 4 → new 3) with the remaining piers carrying the switch without the leaver's vote; the leader-removes-itself edge — it votes in the old side yet the new majority comes from the remaining piers alone, so a ballot of just the leaving leader and one peer fails both sides; neither an old-only nor a new-only quorum smuggles the removal (NoJointMajority); bounded eight → seven.
obs TAME bans clean; the new files carry ≥2 asserts each (not in the zero-assert ratchet). Purely local — no socket, no network, no keys, no funds, no real address ever formed; custody gate #2 real hardware and gate #4 real Kumara both untouched.
